From 1504888ef2f99f10bea83dae56cf7bef1d7f57ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 17:33:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rework projects into per-board pages

Replace the two umbrella pages (MediaTek, Rockchip) with one page per
board, since a board is the unit people actually search for and the unit
SoCBSD organizes arenas around.

Board pages, each grounded in what the work branches actually contain:
- Banana Pi R2 Pro (RK3568 + MT7531): switch driver landed, board routes;
  PCIe disabled, temporary hacks called out honestly
- Banana Pi BPI-R64 (MT7622): mtge ethernet, MT7531 switch, MT7615 wifi
- Banana Pi BPI-R2 (MT7623): clock tree (topgen, infracfg, pericfg, pll,
  hifsys, bdpsys, imgsys, vdecsys, audsys), pinctrl, gpio, syscfg, SMP
- Banana Pi BPI-R3 (MT7986): not started, listed as planned with the
  reuse argument for why it is next

Each board page carries a hardware table, what is done, what is not, and
a link to the branch, so a visitor can tell working from aspirational.

SoCBSD and ports pages get reworked to match: SoCBSD gains a board table
and drops the prose arena list, ports absorbs the Rockchip boot firmware
and recovery tooling section.

The R2 Pro page moves to /projects/bpi-r2-pro.html for naming
consistency; jekyll-redirect-from keeps the old URL alive.

Projects index now groups In progress / Planned / Done and shows the SoC
per board; the homepage leads with the board table.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
